# .claude/ ephemeral subdirs (worktrees, session state, projects).
# .claude/agents/ IS tracked (specialist agent definitions document the workflow).
# .claude/skills/ IS tracked as of 2026-08-16, for the SAME stated reason as agents/.
#   When this rule was written (37049a80, 2026-05-21) skills sat with worktrees/sessions/cache
#   as ephemeral session state. That classification has since decayed: the directory now holds
#   the campaign's operating doctrine (worker-execution, worker-onboarding, advisor-ruling, the
#   two worker onboardings), and CLAUDE.md §11 documents these as project infrastructure where
#   "each encodes a documented production failure" — the exact criterion used to track agents/.
#   They were living on one disk with no version control and no backup.
# ⚠ This creates a SECOND copy: the tracked one here and the runtime surface Claude actually
#   loads from C:\Users\tonio\Projects\trading-forge\.claude\skills. They can drift, exactly as
#   the agent trees did (AR-1258 F-2). The deploy/sync + parity law that closes that is owed
#   under AR-1259 §4.2 and is NOT established by this commit.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/projects/
.claude/local/
.claude/cache/
.claude/sessions/
.claude/state/
.claude/agent-memory/
.claude/commands/
Trading_forge_frontend/amber-vision-main/.claude/

# Operator diagnostic scratch files at repo root (Wave 26 Pass G master close)
/tmp-*.ts

